# Dockerfile.cloudrun.dockerignore — the build context of Dockerfile.cloudrun.
#
# BuildKit uses this file instead of .dockerignore when it builds
# Dockerfile.cloudrun. The local .dockerignore keeps excluding db/, so local
# builds are unchanged.
#
# Allow-list: exclude everything, then let back in only the corpus. The code
# is not taken from this context: Dockerfile.cloudrun starts FROM the local
# image. So .env, venvs, data/, tests/ and any other file in the repo can never
# reach the hosted image, whatever is lying around in the working copy.

*
!db/metadata.db
!db/chroma/
